
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`

-- Código Penal, arts. 138–154-B — what g2b's modules share.
--
-- Written by g2b. Nouns and small readings that more than one of g2b's
-- modules needs, so that each is declared once inside the group. Two of them
-- are marked PROPOSTO-COMUM: other groups need the same thing, and the
-- conductor may hoist them into `cp-dominio.l4` at integration.

§ `Código Penal, arts. 138–154-B — comum ao grupo g2b`

§§ `A execução do crime (art. 14)`

-- The two facts about the execution that art. 14, II reads, beside the
-- element that consummates each crime (which is the crime's own). Whether all
-- the elements of the legal definition are present is decided by each crime's
-- rule and passed to `crime tentado (art. 14, II)` in `cp-pena`.
-- `Execução do crime` is declared in cp-dominio.l4 (integration, 2026-09-30).

§§ `Listas de causas`

-- A cause that applies, or none. Every g2b module lists the causes of
-- increase a case brings into play this way: one `a causa, se incide` per
-- paragraph, then `as causas que incidem` keeps those that do.
-- `a causa se incide` is cp-pena's `a causa, se incide` since integration (2026-09-30).

-- `as causas que incidem` is cp-pena's `as causas que incidem` since integration (2026-09-30).

-- The heavier of two prescribed penalties: the larger maximum, then the
-- larger minimum. Where several qualified forms of one article are present,
-- the heaviest governs and the others weigh in the first phase (art. 59) —
-- the reading g0 took for art. 155 (fork F-g0-18), taken here for arts. 140,
-- 148 and 154-A.
-- `a mais grave das penas`: the heavier of two prescribed penalties (fork F-g0-18) is cp-pena's `a mais grave de duas penas cominadas` since integration (2026-09-30).

-- `a mais grave de todas`: the heaviest of a base and a list of prescribed penalties (fork F-g0-18) is cp-pena's `a mais grave das penas cominadas` since integration (2026-09-30).

§§ `Razões da condição do sexo feminino (art. 121-A, § 1º)`

-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: arts. 92 II, 121-A, 129 § 13, 141 § 3º and 147 § 1º all
-- turn on "contra a mulher por razões da condição do sexo feminino, nos termos
-- do § 1º do art. 121-A". Art. 121-A is g2a's; this is not its rule but the
-- facts its § 1º reads, so that g2b reaches the concept through the noun
-- (PLAN § 6). "§ 1º Considera-se que há razões da condição do sexo feminino
-- quando o crime envolve: I – violência doméstica e familiar; II – menosprezo
-- ou discriminação à condição de mulher."
-- What "violência doméstica e familiar" is, the Code does not say: fork
-- F-sweep-b-08 (g2a creates it; M-sweep-b-17), read here as the fact supplier
-- certifies it.
DECLARE `Razão da condição do sexo feminino` IS ONE OF
    `violência doméstica e familiar`
    @nlg:en the crime involves domestic and family violence
    `menosprezo ou discriminação à condição de mulher`
    @nlg:en the crime involves contempt for, or discrimination against, the condition of being a woman

-- "contra a mulher por razões da condição do sexo feminino": the victim is a
-- woman, and the crime involves I or II of art. 121-A, § 1º.
@ref CP art. 121-A, § 1º, I e II; art. 141, § 3º; art. 147, § 1º
GIVEN v IS A `Vítima`
      `as razões` IS A LIST OF `Razão da condição do sexo feminino`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en the crime is against a woman for reasons of the condition of the female sex, as art. 121-A paragraph 1 defines them
`contra a mulher por razões da condição do sexo feminino (art. 121-A, § 1º)` v `as razões` MEANS
        v's pessoa's mulher
    AND (    "I"  ... elem `violência doméstica e familiar` `as razões`
         OR  "II" ... elem `menosprezo ou discriminação à condição de mulher` `as razões`)

§§ `Cargos que agravam a pena (arts. 141, I e II; 154-A, § 5º)`

-- The offices arts. 141, I–II and 154-A, § 5º name, each in its own words.
-- Record every office the victim held at the time of the fact.
DECLARE `Cargo do ofendido` IS ONE OF
    `Presidente da República`
    @nlg:en the President of the Republic
    `chefe de governo estrangeiro`
    @nlg:en a head of a foreign government
    `governador`
    @nlg:en a state governor
    `prefeito`
    @nlg:en a mayor
    `Presidente do Senado Federal`
    @nlg:en the President of the Federal Senate
    `Presidente da Câmara dos Deputados`
    @nlg:en the President of the Chamber of Deputies
    `Presidente do Supremo Tribunal Federal`
    @nlg:en the President of the Federal Supreme Court
    `Presidente de Assembleia Legislativa de Estado`
    @nlg:en the President of a state Legislative Assembly
    `Presidente da Câmara Legislativa do Distrito Federal`
    @nlg:en the President of the Legislative Chamber of the Federal District
    `Presidente de Câmara Municipal`
    @nlg:en the President of a Municipal Chamber
    `dirigente máximo da administração direta e indireta`
    @nlg:en the highest officer of the direct or indirect federal, state, municipal or Federal District administration

§§ `Funcionário público (art. 327)`

-- Arts. 141, II, 149-A, § 1º, I and 150 (fork F-sweep-b-04) need to know
-- whether a person is a "funcionário público". Integration, 2026-09-30: the
-- local reading that stood here (caput and both limbs of § 1º, with no date)
-- is deleted; the callers call g6a's owner rule, `funcionário público para os
-- efeitos penais (art. 327)` in `cp-g6a-funcionario-publico.l4`, with the
-- fact's date, under the conductor's ruling on § 1º's vigência (F-g6a-23).

§§ `Emprego de arma (arts. 146, § 1º; 147-A, § 1º, III; 150, § 1º)`

-- "há emprego de armas" (art. 146, § 1º), "com o emprego de arma" (arts.
-- 147-A, § 1º, III and 150, § 1º): "arma" unqualified. Read as any weapon,
-- proper or improper — a firearm of either class, a bladed weapon, or another
-- object used as a weapon — and one is enough for art. 146's plural "armas"
-- (fork F-g2b-05). A toy or replica is not a weapon: Súmula 174 STJ, which
-- held the contrary for roubo, was cancelled (M-sweep-b-39).
@ref CP art. 146, § 1º; art. 147-A, § 1º, III; art. 150, § 1º
GIVEN meios IS A LIST OF `Meio empregado`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg:en a weapon was used, proper or improper
`com o emprego de arma` meios MEANS
        elem `emprego de arma branca` meios
    ..  elem `emprego de arma de fogo de uso permitido` meios
    ..  elem `emprego de arma de fogo de uso restrito ou proibido` meios
    OR  elem `emprego de outro objeto como arma` meios
